    "question": {
      ":question/id": "abe2b8c2-bdbe-54ac-81cd-971c9e06756b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(- 4 y)\\,i+(- 4 x + 2 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- 4 t + 3)\\,i+(- 3 t - 2)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- 4 t + 3,\\quad y=- 3 t - 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 4 y)\\,i+(- 4 x + 2 y)\\,j \\\\  & =(12 t + 8)\\,i+(10 t - 16)\\,j \\\\  & =(12 t + 8)\\,i+(10 t - 16)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t + 3)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t - 2)\\,j \\\\  & =(-4)\\,i+(-3)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((12 t + 8)\\,i+(10 t - 16)\\,j)\\cdot((-4)\\,i+(-3)\\,j) \\\\  & =(12 t + 8)\\cdot(-4)+(10 t - 16)\\cdot(-3) \\\\  & =(- 48 t - 32)+(- 30 t + 48) \\\\  & =- 78 t + 16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}(- 78 t + 16)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[- 39 t^{2} + 16 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((-39)+(16))-((0)+(0)) \\\\  & =(-23)-(0) \\\\  & =-23\\end{aligned}\n$$",
