      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}F\\cdot\\text{d}r$ given that $F(x,y)=(2 y)\\,i+(- 3 x + 4 y)\\,j$ and $C$ is the path $r(t)=(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+(- 2 t - 3)\\,j$ for $t\\in[0,1].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=- 4 t - 4,\\quad y=- 2 t - 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(2 y)\\,i+(- 3 x + 4 y)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 4 t - 6)\\,i+(4 t)\\,j \\\\  & =(- 4 t - 6)\\,i+(4 t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 4 t - 4)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t - 3)\\,j \\\\  & =(-4)\\,i+(-2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((- 4 t - 6)\\,i+(4 t)\\,j)\\cdot((-4)\\,i+(-2)\\,j) \\\\  & =(- 4 t - 6)\\cdot(-4)+(4 t)\\cdot(-2) \\\\  & =(16 t + 24)+(- 8 t) \\\\  & =8 t + 24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}(8 t + 24)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[4 t^{2} + 24 t\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((4)+(24))-((0)+(0)) \\\\  & =(28)-(0) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$",
