      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r=\\int_a^b F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=2 t^{2},\\quad y=- 3 t^{3} - 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =(- 2 x y - 4 y)\\,i+(4 x^{2} + 2 y)\\,j \\\\  & =(12 t^{3} - 4 t^{2} \\left(- 3 t^{3} - 4\\right) + 16)\\,i+(16 t^{4} - 6 t^{3} - 8)\\,j \\\\  & =(12 t^{5} + 12 t^{3} + 16 t^{2} + 16)\\,i+(16 t^{4} - 6 t^{3} - 8)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $r^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r^{\\prime}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t^{3} - 4)\\,j \\\\  & =(4 t)\\,i+(- 9 t^{2})\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t) & =((12 t^{5} + 12 t^{3} + 16 t^{2} + 16)\\,i+(16 t^{4} - 6 t^{3} - 8)\\,j)\\cdot((4 t)\\,i+(- 9 t^{2})\\,j) \\\\  & =(12 t^{5} + 12 t^{3} + 16 t^{2} + 16)\\cdot(4 t)+(16 t^{4} - 6 t^{3} - 8)\\cdot(- 9 t^{2}) \\\\  & =(48 t^{6} + 48 t^{4} + 64 t^{3} + 64 t)+(- 144 t^{6} + 54 t^{5} + 72 t^{2}) \\\\  & =2 t \\left(- 48 t^{5} + 27 t^{4} + 24 t^{3} + 32 t^{2} + 36 t + 32\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C F\\cdot\\text{d}r & =\\int_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot r^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int_{0}^{1}(2 t \\left(- 48 t^{5} + 27 t^{4} + 24 t^{3} + 32 t^{2} + 36 t + 32\\right))\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\left[- \\frac{96 t^{7}}{7} + 9 t^{6} + \\frac{48 t^{5}}{5} + 16 t^{4} + 24 t^{3} + 32 t^{2}\\right]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((9)+(16)+(24)+(32)+(- \\frac{96}{7})+(\\frac{48}{5}))-((0)+(0)+(0)+(0)+(0)+(0)) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2691}{35})-(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2691}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
